[6] THE STATEMENT S2 ACTUALLY IS -- and it is verified on the whole census
   (S2)  Let c >= 1 and let tail be a weakly-decreasing list of integers in [0,c]
         with c + sum(tail) ODD.  Put  L = W-(c) u tail  and  L' = W+(c+1) u tail.
         If the Havel-Hakimi runs of L and of L' both terminate, then
                        0 <= R(L) - R(L') <= 1.
   Note |L'| = |L| + 1 and sum(L') = sum(L) + 2c + 4: these are TWO SEPARATELY
   CONSTRUCTED lists, NOT one list and a perturbation of it.
